WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.200
Your code is a forest.
[A pine forest at dawn, a lookout tower on the hill.]

2
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:11.200
Your agents plant fast. Every package is a tree.
[Trees pop up one by one in the foreground, each with a package name.]

3
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:16.600
On the horizon, a thin smoke: a known vulnerability.
[A thin thread of smoke rises behind the farthest ridge.]

4
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.200
Nobody is looking. The lookout is.
[The beam of the lookout tower lands on the smoke.]

5
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:27.600
Install blocked, before it lands.
[The real Vigie report appears: install of lodash 4.17.20 blocked, 4 known vulnerabilities.]

6
00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:34.200
The report tells your agent what to do.
[The line "What to do: Upgrade lodash to 4.18.0 or later" is highlighted; the four sources answer ok.]

7
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:39.600
The agent fixes it. The forest stays safe.
[The lodash 4.18.0 tree is planted; day breaks, the tower keeps watching.]

8
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:47.000
Vigie. Your agent checks known vulnerabilities, every time. Free, Open source (MIT), No account.
[The forest in the morning, the name Vigie. OSV.dev · CISA KEV · EPSS · CERT-FR. Publicly known vulnerabilities in published packages only.]
